WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.402 --> 00:00:02.594
- I BS'd my way into
jobs that I didn't have

00:00:02.594 --> 00:00:05.026
the experience to do, and pulled it off.

00:00:05.026 --> 00:00:06.312
But I had to believe in myself

00:00:06.312 --> 00:00:07.982
to BS my way into a job.

00:00:07.982 --> 00:00:10.937
- There's no place for
patience in business.

00:00:10.937 --> 00:00:14.220
Patience in life means things happen

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.566
slower than they could.

00:00:16.566 --> 00:00:17.759
- The last thing you want to do

00:00:17.759 --> 00:00:19.977
is open a bar because you like to drink.

00:00:19.977 --> 00:00:22.040
That's like somebody into drugs

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.263
who becomes a pharmacist.

00:00:23.263 --> 00:00:24.252
I mean, that's just.

00:00:24.252 --> 00:00:25.662
(audience laughs)

00:00:25.662 --> 00:00:27.624
- Hello Believe Nation,
I'm Evan Carmichael.

00:00:27.624 --> 00:00:30.188
My one word is believe, and I believe

00:00:30.188 --> 00:00:31.725
that entrepreneurs are going to solve

00:00:31.725 --> 00:00:34.159
all of the major problems of the world.

00:00:34.159 --> 00:00:35.292
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:35.292 --> 00:00:36.308
today we're going to learn from

00:00:36.308 --> 00:00:38.694
Bar Rescue TV host and world-renowned

00:00:38.694 --> 00:00:40.527
bar expert Jon Taffer,

00:00:41.411 --> 00:00:44.676
and my take on his top
ten rules for success.

00:00:44.676 --> 00:00:46.428
Rule number two is my personal favorite,

00:00:46.428 --> 00:00:47.345
and I'd love to know which one

00:00:47.345 --> 00:00:48.979
you guys like the best.

00:00:48.979 --> 00:00:50.491
And as always guys, as you're watching,

00:00:50.491 --> 00:00:51.731
if you hear something that really

00:00:51.731 --> 00:00:53.622
resonates with you, please leave it down

00:00:53.622 --> 00:00:54.648
in the comments below.

00:00:54.648 --> 00:00:55.966
Put quotes around it so other people

00:00:55.966 --> 00:00:57.139
can be inspired.

00:00:57.139 --> 00:00:58.725
And when you write it down

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:02.186
it's more likely to stick
for yourself as well.

00:01:02.186 --> 00:01:03.309
Enjoy.

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:05.978
(swoosh sound)

00:01:05.978 --> 00:01:08.645
(intense music)

00:01:16.161 --> 00:01:18.999
- You wake up in the
morning, you're failing.

00:01:18.999 --> 00:01:20.878
So you blame the president,
you blame congress,

00:01:20.878 --> 00:01:23.638
you blame Greece, blame the euro.

00:01:23.638 --> 00:01:27.228
Construction in the
street, it's the mayor, oh.

00:01:27.228 --> 00:01:28.303
And you wake up in the morning

00:01:28.303 --> 00:01:29.739
and you look in the mirror,

00:01:29.739 --> 00:01:30.942
and you're not failing because

00:01:30.942 --> 00:01:32.542
it's the other guy's fault.

00:01:32.542 --> 00:01:33.895
Or it's the economy's fault.

00:01:33.895 --> 00:01:35.332
But if you looked in the mirror

00:01:35.332 --> 00:01:37.504
and said, "I'm failing because of me,"

00:01:37.504 --> 00:01:40.370
you wouldn't like it
and you'd change that.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:42.901
I believe the common
denominator of failure

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:45.345
in any business is excuses.

00:01:45.345 --> 00:01:47.994
As long as you wake up
and blame poor sales

00:01:47.994 --> 00:01:50.055
on the economy or an environment,

00:01:50.055 --> 00:01:53.025
then you have no motivation
to make it better.

00:01:53.025 --> 00:01:54.646
Because it's not your fault.

00:01:54.646 --> 00:01:57.315
But in the worst economic environment,

00:01:57.315 --> 00:01:58.438
four or five years ago in this country

00:01:58.438 --> 00:02:01.565
that we've seen in our lifetimes,

00:02:01.565 --> 00:02:04.262
there were people making a
lot of money, weren't there?

00:02:04.262 --> 00:02:05.667
In the height of that
recession were people

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.756
selling advertising,
people opening restaurants,

00:02:07.756 --> 00:02:08.874
people building businesses.

00:02:08.874 --> 00:02:12.364
Somebody's making money,
so the excuse is bull.

00:02:12.364 --> 00:02:13.621
It's bull.

00:02:13.621 --> 00:02:16.229
So wake up in the morning
and own your failure.

00:02:16.229 --> 00:02:17.062
Look in the mirror and say,

00:02:17.062 --> 00:02:18.959
"I'm failing because of me."

00:02:18.959 --> 00:02:20.310
And you won't like it.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:21.783
And then you'll change it.

00:02:21.783 --> 00:02:24.161
But as long as you don't put it on you,

00:02:24.161 --> 00:02:25.973
you have no motivation to change it.

00:02:25.973 --> 00:02:28.793
So in short, if you own your failure,

00:02:28.793 --> 00:02:30.297
you'll own your success.

00:02:30.297 --> 00:02:31.879
If you don't own your failure,

00:02:31.879 --> 00:02:33.179
you'll never dig out.

00:02:33.179 --> 00:02:34.995
I find that in any business;

00:02:34.995 --> 00:02:37.427
always the common denominator of failure

00:02:37.427 --> 00:02:39.260
personally is excuses.

00:02:40.112 --> 00:02:41.772
You don't want to be a failure, do you?

00:02:41.772 --> 00:02:42.605
- [Audience Member] Not at all.

00:02:42.605 --> 00:02:43.581
- You don't want to look in the mirror

00:02:43.581 --> 00:02:45.057
and experience that.

00:02:45.057 --> 00:02:47.099
If you can't blame anybody but yourself,

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:48.572
you're going to change.

00:02:48.572 --> 00:02:50.782
You're going to fight
it out, that's the deal.

00:02:50.782 --> 00:02:53.134
I BS'd my way into jobs that I didn't have

00:02:53.134 --> 00:02:55.358
the experience to do, and pulled it off.

00:02:55.358 --> 00:02:56.694
But I had to believe in myself

00:02:56.694 --> 00:02:58.543
to BS my way into a job.

00:02:58.543 --> 00:03:00.278
When you were younger you didn't have

00:03:00.278 --> 00:03:01.826
the producer experience you have now.

00:03:01.826 --> 00:03:03.094
- No, but I always had the confidence

00:03:03.094 --> 00:03:04.560
like I can do it, I'll figure it out.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.953
- Exactly right, and I knew
I could figure it out too.

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:07.786
- [Evan] Right.

00:03:07.786 --> 00:03:08.619
- And that gave me the confidence

00:03:08.619 --> 00:03:11.013
to show up at the interview
and convince that guy

00:03:11.013 --> 00:03:14.170
to hire me because I was convinced myself

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:15.312
that I could do it.

00:03:15.312 --> 00:03:16.949
And that comes across.

00:03:16.949 --> 00:03:19.985
Let me introduce you to
the concept of success.

00:03:19.985 --> 00:03:21.779
Ben Franklin was a pretty smart guy,

00:03:21.779 --> 00:03:24.353
and I want to start with a quote by him.

00:03:24.353 --> 00:03:26.834
"If you do tomorrow what you did today,

00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:30.084
"you will get tomorrow
what you got today."

00:03:30.084 --> 00:03:31.992
You want to know what that means?

00:03:31.992 --> 00:03:33.518
The average American makes between

00:03:33.518 --> 00:03:35.703
three and five percent more each year.

00:03:35.703 --> 00:03:37.202
That's the deal.

00:03:37.202 --> 00:03:39.034
In today's economy, I'm not
sure we're going to make

00:03:39.034 --> 00:03:40.480
the three to four to five percent

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:42.238
next year as employees.

00:03:42.238 --> 00:03:45.045
So it takes you 20 years
to double your income

00:03:45.045 --> 00:03:47.678
in America as an average person.

00:03:47.678 --> 00:03:49.288
That's the mediocrity that

00:03:49.288 --> 00:03:51.334
we're stuck in in life.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:52.385
And then you meet people who have

00:03:52.385 --> 00:03:55.706
the uncanny ability to double
their income in a year.

00:03:55.706 --> 00:03:58.325
To get promoted five times in a year.

00:03:58.325 --> 00:03:59.996
The ones that beat the system.

00:03:59.996 --> 00:04:01.400
The ones that conquer it.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.933
You've all seen them, haven't you?

00:04:03.933 --> 00:04:05.734
The difference between them and the ones

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:07.575
that don't do that is that they wake up

00:04:07.575 --> 00:04:11.038
in the morning, and
they think differently.

00:04:11.038 --> 00:04:12.941
They understand that if i do tomorrow

00:04:12.941 --> 00:04:14.877
what I did today, I'm
going to get tomorrow

00:04:14.877 --> 00:04:16.151
what I got today.

00:04:16.151 --> 00:04:18.291
You want a bigger car?

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:20.460
- How about a nice house in Tahiti?

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.764
Sherri, would you love a nice house

00:04:21.764 --> 00:04:23.025
in the Hills?

00:04:23.025 --> 00:04:25.721
We all want better things don't we?

00:04:25.721 --> 00:04:28.131
We all want more friends,
more stuff, more money,

00:04:28.131 --> 00:04:31.608
more security, more
travel, more enjoyment.

00:04:31.608 --> 00:04:33.674
If you do the same thing tomorrow

00:04:33.674 --> 00:04:36.581
that you did today, you're stuck.

00:04:36.581 --> 00:04:38.078
Stuck.

00:04:38.078 --> 00:04:40.083
And it doesn't change.

00:04:40.083 --> 00:04:41.988
And it grows a little at a time.

00:04:41.988 --> 00:04:44.191
And you get a taste of success,

00:04:44.191 --> 00:04:46.058
but it's never fast enough.

00:04:46.058 --> 00:04:48.484
It never excites you, and when it does

00:04:48.484 --> 00:04:49.522
it's a good month.

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:51.749
Or a good two months,
or a good three months.

00:04:51.749 --> 00:04:54.321
But it doesn't provide a trajectory

00:04:54.321 --> 00:04:56.000
that creates success.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.195
So the first thing I want you

00:04:57.195 --> 00:04:59.801
to think about today,
is I want you to wake up

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:02.540
tomorrow and do something different.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:05.103
Understand if you do the same damn thing,

00:05:05.103 --> 00:05:06.186
you're stuck.

00:05:07.465 --> 00:05:10.077
Just because you did it
a certain way yesterday

00:05:10.077 --> 00:05:13.201
is no reason to do it that way today.

00:05:13.201 --> 00:05:14.893
I want it to hit hard.

00:05:14.893 --> 00:05:17.883
That's not what drives success, you do.

00:05:17.883 --> 00:05:18.736
You do.

00:05:18.736 --> 00:05:20.271
And you do.

00:05:20.271 --> 00:05:21.293
When you go back tomorrow,

00:05:21.293 --> 00:05:24.189
you'll either start counting
guests or you won't.

00:05:24.189 --> 00:05:25.579
You'll either look at
your marketing budget

00:05:25.579 --> 00:05:27.909
and split it up to new
frequency or expenditure

00:05:27.909 --> 00:05:29.494
or you won't.

00:05:29.494 --> 00:05:31.207
You'll either look at your staff

00:05:31.207 --> 00:05:32.690
and get rid of the dead
weight that you know

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:35.518
is costing you money, or you won't.

00:05:35.518 --> 00:05:37.040
And you'll look at your bar programs

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:39.452
and what to do, or you won't.

00:05:39.452 --> 00:05:41.547
Everyone of you wrote the word action down

00:05:41.547 --> 00:05:43.629
at least a few times, correct?

00:05:43.629 --> 00:05:44.493
(audience agrees)

00:05:44.493 --> 00:05:45.964
Do it.

00:05:45.964 --> 00:05:47.342
Do it.

00:05:47.342 --> 00:05:48.725
You know I'm just not patient.

00:05:48.725 --> 00:05:51.673
There's no place for patience in business.

00:05:51.673 --> 00:05:55.065
Patience in life means things happen

00:05:55.065 --> 00:05:57.776
slower than they could.

00:05:57.776 --> 00:05:59.441
So if you're going to be on this planet

00:05:59.441 --> 00:06:02.572
for 70 years and things happen slower

00:06:02.572 --> 00:06:04.933
than they should, at the end of 70 years

00:06:04.933 --> 00:06:07.438
you're going to have less, aren't you?

00:06:07.438 --> 00:06:09.802
Less experiences, less time, less money,

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:11.624
less of everything.

00:06:11.624 --> 00:06:13.188
So let's all hurry up, man,

00:06:13.188 --> 00:06:14.579
and get more out of life.

00:06:14.579 --> 00:06:15.605
That's my view.

00:06:15.605 --> 00:06:17.643
- So patience is not a--
- Am I crazy?

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:19.290
(audience applauds)

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:21.705
If you think your life is complete,

00:06:21.705 --> 00:06:24.132
then I suggest that you're an ass.

00:06:24.132 --> 00:06:27.575
Because tomorrow always has
a great opportunity in it.

00:06:27.575 --> 00:06:28.802
Your life is not complete

00:06:28.802 --> 00:06:30.677
until you close your eyes.

00:06:30.677 --> 00:06:34.008
So when you say somebody
who's in a job they hate

00:06:34.008 --> 00:06:36.238
would love to be able to do this,

00:06:36.238 --> 00:06:39.249
my comment is why the hell
are you in a job you hate?

00:06:39.249 --> 00:06:41.135
Don't you have the courage to leave it?

00:06:41.135 --> 00:06:42.266
So you're in a job you hate,

00:06:42.266 --> 00:06:43.398
you're doing nothing to change it,

00:06:43.398 --> 00:06:45.272
but you'd like better?

00:06:45.272 --> 00:06:46.497
You have to do better.

00:06:46.497 --> 00:06:47.590
- Sometimes if they have mouths to feed,

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:48.975
sometimes I get it.

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:52.443
But what were the things about you?

00:06:52.443 --> 00:06:53.442
Listen, we'd have to go over those

00:06:53.442 --> 00:06:55.513
specific cases I think,
and really getting into

00:06:55.513 --> 00:06:56.877
each person to break them.

00:06:56.877 --> 00:06:58.897
But what do you think
were the things about you?

00:06:58.897 --> 00:07:00.822
One of it is you always had your eyes

00:07:00.822 --> 00:07:02.695
open to tomorrow and new opportunities.

00:07:02.695 --> 00:07:04.533
What were some of the other things

00:07:04.533 --> 00:07:05.905
as part of your personality,

00:07:05.905 --> 00:07:07.915
because there aren't many people like you,

00:07:07.915 --> 00:07:10.473
but I've seen and I'm
studying more and more people

00:07:10.473 --> 00:07:12.989
where amazing things are
happening at 55 and 60,

00:07:12.989 --> 00:07:14.285
and putting them on life journeys

00:07:14.285 --> 00:07:16.179
that they never thought
they were going to have.

00:07:16.179 --> 00:07:17.829
And I'm seeing that you guys

00:07:17.829 --> 00:07:21.081
have a lot of the similar
attributes, but what do you think?

00:07:21.081 --> 00:07:22.823
What was it about you, Jon?

00:07:22.823 --> 00:07:24.290
- Courage.

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:25.426
Courage.

00:07:25.426 --> 00:07:27.114
The first time I went and shot a pilot

00:07:27.114 --> 00:07:30.301
for Bar Rescue, it was really hard.

00:07:30.301 --> 00:07:31.840
You think it's easy to scream at people

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:33.193
on national television?

00:07:33.193 --> 00:07:35.150
To insult people on national television?

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:37.118
To call you a jerk,
challenge your marriage,

00:07:37.118 --> 00:07:39.740
challenge your integrity,

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:41.274
challenge your professionalism?

00:07:41.274 --> 00:07:42.732
That's hard.

00:07:42.732 --> 00:07:44.161
That's not who I am.

00:07:44.161 --> 00:07:45.398
I don't wake up and embarrass people

00:07:45.398 --> 00:07:46.558
in front of their friends.

00:07:46.558 --> 00:07:47.391
- [Evan] Right.

00:07:47.391 --> 00:07:48.308
- In front of their family.

00:07:48.308 --> 00:07:51.695
Bar Rescue is the hardest
work I have ever done.

00:07:51.695 --> 00:07:53.916
The courage that it takes
for me to go out there

00:07:53.916 --> 00:07:55.427
and do these things.

00:07:55.427 --> 00:07:58.842
When I was in my young 20s
I was managing expenses,

00:07:58.842 --> 00:08:00.655
managing marketing budgets,

00:08:00.655 --> 00:08:02.812
and faced a lot of the
problems that you did.

00:08:02.812 --> 00:08:05.512
My labor cost was too
high, so I'm shaving hours.

00:08:05.512 --> 00:08:06.976
My marketing expense is too high,

00:08:06.976 --> 00:08:08.570
so I'm shaving dimes.

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:09.945
I can't give stuff away,

00:08:09.945 --> 00:08:11.635
I have less dollars for entertainment.

00:08:11.635 --> 00:08:13.026
Suddenly my rent is expensive,

00:08:13.026 --> 00:08:16.313
my occupancy cost is expensive,
my taxes are expensive.

00:08:16.313 --> 00:08:17.729
And I'm just focused on the fact

00:08:17.729 --> 00:08:19.386
that everything is expensive.

00:08:19.386 --> 00:08:20.946
Then somebody came into my business

00:08:20.946 --> 00:08:22.505
and taught me how to do a promotion.

00:08:22.505 --> 00:08:23.786
Literally a month later,

00:08:23.786 --> 00:08:25.787
my revenues went up 30%.

00:08:25.787 --> 00:08:26.704
In a month.

00:08:27.988 --> 00:08:30.307
When I looked at my PNL,

00:08:30.307 --> 00:08:31.787
I didn't have a labor cost problem.

00:08:31.787 --> 00:08:32.929
The numbers worked.

00:08:32.929 --> 00:08:35.250
Suddenly I had a few
dollars for marketing.

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:36.944
I could actually buy some stuff.

00:08:36.944 --> 00:08:38.814
I had money for new paint on the walls,

00:08:38.814 --> 00:08:41.172
and I realized that day

00:08:41.172 --> 00:08:44.288
we don't have expense
problems in any business.

00:08:44.288 --> 00:08:46.652
All we have are revenue problems.

00:08:46.652 --> 00:08:48.344
Revenue is the cure-all;

00:08:48.344 --> 00:08:49.772
that's the asprin you take every night

00:08:49.772 --> 00:08:50.982
to feel better in the morning

00:08:50.982 --> 00:08:53.703
is revenue, revenue, revenue.

00:08:53.703 --> 00:08:56.047
You got to wake up in the
morning and drive revenue,

00:08:56.047 --> 00:08:58.415
which means you got to have
the promotions, the ideas,

00:08:58.415 --> 00:09:00.973
the energy to elevate a business.

00:09:00.973 --> 00:09:04.032
You got to be a rainmaker in business,

00:09:04.032 --> 00:09:06.229
or you're never going to get anyone wet.

00:09:06.229 --> 00:09:07.957
And when they don't get wet,

00:09:07.957 --> 00:09:10.636
they dry up and go away.

00:09:10.636 --> 00:09:12.986
It's that wetness of a rainmaker

00:09:12.986 --> 00:09:15.971
that filters down and trickles

00:09:15.971 --> 00:09:17.731
to everybody's success.

00:09:17.731 --> 00:09:19.758
You have to drive the energy of revenue

00:09:19.758 --> 00:09:21.661
to be successful, and when you do,

00:09:21.661 --> 00:09:23.397
you'll have no expense problems.

00:09:23.397 --> 00:09:25.573
Anybody see the Murphy's
episode of Bar Rescue?

00:09:25.573 --> 00:09:27.213
The two frat brothers who opened a bar?

00:09:27.213 --> 00:09:28.046
- Yeah.

00:09:28.046 --> 00:09:29.008
- The last thing you want to do

00:09:29.008 --> 00:09:31.069
is open a bar because you like to drink.

00:09:31.069 --> 00:09:33.627
That's like somebody into drugs

00:09:33.627 --> 00:09:34.583
who becomes a pharmacist.

00:09:34.583 --> 00:09:35.864
I mean, that's just.

00:09:35.864 --> 00:09:37.181
(audience laughs)

00:09:37.181 --> 00:09:38.458
It makes no sense at all.

00:09:38.458 --> 00:09:40.143
You got to do it for the right reasons,

00:09:40.143 --> 00:09:42.168
You got to do it because
you love the business.

00:09:42.168 --> 00:09:43.991
If you love the social aspect of it,

00:09:43.991 --> 00:09:45.358
you'll never do your financials,

00:09:45.358 --> 00:09:47.428
you'll just hang with people all day long.

00:09:47.428 --> 00:09:49.517
If you love the drinking,
that's even worse.

00:09:49.517 --> 00:09:51.003
You got to love the business,

00:09:51.003 --> 00:09:52.279
it's a tough business.

00:09:52.279 --> 00:09:54.222
We were talking before we started.

00:09:54.222 --> 00:09:56.081
In a clothing store
business, you buy shirts,

00:09:56.081 --> 00:09:58.370
you mark them up 60, 70%.

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:00.070
If you've got ten shirts on the shelf,

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:01.432
you go home that night, you come back

00:10:01.432 --> 00:10:02.626
in the morning and you
still got ten shirts

00:10:02.626 --> 00:10:03.459
on the shelf.

00:10:03.459 --> 00:10:04.490
Not the bar business.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:07.315
Bar business, you've go
to manage every minute.

00:10:07.315 --> 00:10:08.624
Right product is exposed,

00:10:08.624 --> 00:10:09.998
liabilities are exposed.

00:10:09.998 --> 00:10:11.842
It's a tough business.

00:10:11.842 --> 00:10:13.760
Honestly, if I had to do it over again,

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:15.387
I'm not sure I would be in this business.

00:10:15.387 --> 00:10:16.803
To be honest with you,

00:10:16.803 --> 00:10:19.568
when I look at all the work
that I did over the years,

00:10:19.568 --> 00:10:21.341
I could have applied those efforts

00:10:21.341 --> 00:10:24.933
to bigger things rather than smaller bars.

00:10:24.933 --> 00:10:27.175
I was involved in
Rainforest Cafe for example.

00:10:27.175 --> 00:10:28.926
That went public and that was big dollars.

00:10:28.926 --> 00:10:30.482
Don't get me wrong, I don't regret

00:10:30.482 --> 00:10:33.240
being in a bar business,
but when I look at my life,

00:10:33.240 --> 00:10:36.710
all the nights that I
worked, all those evenings,

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:38.848
days, 20-hour days, I look back and say,

00:10:38.848 --> 00:10:41.179
"Gee, what if I'd have been a lawyer?"

00:10:41.179 --> 00:10:42.012
Nah, maybe not a lawyer.

00:10:42.012 --> 00:10:43.443
(audience laughter)

00:10:43.443 --> 00:10:46.637
There are lifestyles that
are easier is my point.

00:10:46.637 --> 00:10:48.829
So you got to love the
business and be passionate

00:10:48.829 --> 00:10:50.818
about it to make it
through those late nights

00:10:50.818 --> 00:10:52.023
and those mornings.

00:10:52.023 --> 00:10:54.155
I have a dear friend who
works for a large company

00:10:54.155 --> 00:10:55.782
and he wants to open a franchise,

00:10:55.782 --> 00:10:58.011
buy a franchise, of sandwich stores.

00:10:58.011 --> 00:10:59.221
I won't say which brand.

00:10:59.221 --> 00:11:01.037
He wants to buy it with a territory.

00:11:01.037 --> 00:11:02.151
He meets with me and he says,

00:11:02.151 --> 00:11:03.625
"Jon I need some advice,

00:11:03.625 --> 00:11:07.792
"do I leave my long-standing
job and benefits and do this?"

00:11:09.083 --> 00:11:11.054
So why can't you have
your cake and eat it too?

00:11:11.054 --> 00:11:11.997
- [Evan] Right.

00:11:11.997 --> 00:11:13.197
- Why can't you bring in a partner,

00:11:13.197 --> 00:11:14.818
why can't you bring in somebody to do it?

00:11:14.818 --> 00:11:16.992
There's ways to get there.

00:11:16.992 --> 00:11:18.934
It doesn't have to be absolute.

00:11:18.934 --> 00:11:21.421
If somebody wants to create a 2nd career,

00:11:21.421 --> 00:11:24.081
create new opportunities in their life,

00:11:24.081 --> 00:11:26.894
figure out a way to do it
without risking what you have.

00:11:26.894 --> 00:11:27.815
- [Evan] Right.

00:11:27.815 --> 00:11:29.550
- And if you want it enough,

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:30.777
you'll figure it out.

00:11:30.777 --> 00:11:33.826
Everything that we do
is reaction management.

00:11:33.826 --> 00:11:35.253
If you can make your bosses

00:11:35.253 --> 00:11:37.507
react the way you want them to,

00:11:37.507 --> 00:11:39.807
you're going to get a
promotion aren't you?

00:11:39.807 --> 00:11:41.402
You're going to get that job you want.

00:11:41.402 --> 00:11:43.878
How do you get them to
react to you in a way

00:11:43.878 --> 00:11:45.656
that gets you promoted?

00:11:45.656 --> 00:11:48.471
When you figure that
out, you'll get promoted.

00:11:48.471 --> 00:11:50.152
That's reaction management.

00:11:50.152 --> 00:11:52.730
It's understanding that those reactions

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:54.957
that happen around you drive your future

00:11:54.957 --> 00:11:56.401
more than you do.

00:11:56.401 --> 00:11:58.266
The only final advice I would give you

00:11:58.266 --> 00:12:00.884
is I've lived a very unconventional life,

00:12:00.884 --> 00:12:04.760
and it's because I live
my dream every day.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:07.593
Dreams are inspiring, work is not.

00:12:08.873 --> 00:12:10.396
Find a dream.

00:12:10.396 --> 00:12:12.745
Whether it's that client you can't get

00:12:12.745 --> 00:12:15.056
that you've been fighting
for for six months.

00:12:15.056 --> 00:12:16.988
You've got to have dreams.

00:12:16.988 --> 00:12:18.515
Dreams make this world go on,

00:12:18.515 --> 00:12:20.258
it built our whole country.

00:12:20.258 --> 00:12:24.375
And when we get in a rut as human beings,

00:12:24.375 --> 00:12:26.946
is when we lose touch with our dreams.

00:12:26.946 --> 00:12:29.185
We lose the ability to
fight for those dreams.

00:12:29.185 --> 00:12:31.465
So don't be an employee of Google.

00:12:31.465 --> 00:12:33.676
Live your dreams at Google.

00:12:33.676 --> 00:12:36.426
Find the way to match your dreams

00:12:37.302 --> 00:12:39.754
with the goals of your
company in your own work.

00:12:39.754 --> 00:12:41.780
Because there's nothing worse

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:44.960
than mechanical employees that lost touch

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:46.177
with their dream.

00:12:46.177 --> 00:12:48.599
The worst thing in the
world is when you see

00:12:48.599 --> 00:12:52.099
somebody who lost touch with their dreams.

00:12:53.628 --> 00:12:55.126
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:12:55.126 --> 00:12:57.375
I made this video because Shredder Steve

00:12:57.375 --> 00:12:58.424
asked me to.

00:12:58.424 --> 00:12:59.486
So if there's someone
you'd like me to cover

00:12:59.486 --> 00:13:02.116
in the next top ten,
please check out the link

00:13:02.116 --> 00:13:04.473
in the description so
you can cast your vote.

00:13:04.473 --> 00:13:05.548
I also want to give a quick shout-out

00:13:05.548 --> 00:13:06.841
to Tanya Jackson.

00:13:06.841 --> 00:13:07.768
Tanya, thank you so much

00:13:07.768 --> 00:13:09.111
for picking up a copy of my book,

00:13:09.111 --> 00:13:10.304
"Your One Word" and posting

00:13:10.304 --> 00:13:11.917
that awesome picture on Twitter.

00:13:11.917 --> 00:13:13.562
I really, really appreciate it

00:13:13.562 --> 00:13:14.938
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:13:14.938 --> 00:13:16.401
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:13:16.401 --> 00:13:17.625
I believe in you.

00:13:17.625 --> 00:13:19.721
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:13:19.721 --> 00:13:22.313
and whatever your one word is.

00:13:22.313 --> 00:13:24.733
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:13:24.733 --> 00:13:28.900
(zoom sound followed by explosion)

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:32.692
- I drive quality as a leader,

00:13:32.692 --> 00:13:34.967
my systems maintain quality.

00:13:34.967 --> 00:13:37.209
Now with regard to new projects,

00:13:37.209 --> 00:13:39.841
to me, every new project is a ball.

00:13:39.841 --> 00:13:42.535
I have to move that ball every day.

00:13:42.535 --> 00:13:45.169
So I know, for example,
that I have four balls

00:13:45.169 --> 00:13:46.002
on my desk.

00:13:46.002 --> 00:13:47.348
They might be five pads.

00:13:47.348 --> 00:13:48.810
Let's say five balls on my desk.

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:50.669
They might be five different pads,

00:13:50.669 --> 00:13:52.612
five different books,
five different projects.

00:13:52.612 --> 00:13:55.485
Every day I'm going to
move those five balls.

00:13:55.485 --> 00:13:57.556
That's the way I live my life,

00:13:57.556 --> 00:13:59.792
and I can't go to sleep
at night if I don't move

00:13:59.792 --> 00:14:02.432
every one of those five balls every day.

00:14:02.432 --> 00:14:03.736
Sometimes I have three balls,

00:14:03.736 --> 00:14:04.871
sometimes I have seven balls,

00:14:04.871 --> 00:14:07.663
but the amount of balls that I accept

00:14:07.663 --> 00:14:10.056
and put on my desk, every one of them

00:14:10.056 --> 00:14:11.941
is going to move forward every day.

00:14:11.941 --> 00:14:13.980
And I become relentless.

00:14:13.980 --> 00:14:16.304
I've learned to live my life based upon

00:14:16.304 --> 00:14:19.109
the progress I make on a daily basis.

00:14:19.109 --> 00:14:21.854
And I believe that business is defined

00:14:21.854 --> 00:14:24.998
by what we do every day, every single day.

00:14:24.998 --> 00:14:28.275
And business is defined
by the days that we have.

00:14:28.275 --> 00:14:31.868
So if you move those five balls every day,

00:14:31.868 --> 00:14:33.482
you can't help but be successful.

00:14:33.482 --> 00:14:34.599
You will achieve it,

00:14:34.599 --> 00:14:37.849
but you'll achieve it on a daily basis.

